<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ajax the Lesser</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Locrian Ajax</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ajax the Lesser is a hero of Greek mythology, son of Oileus and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locrians">Locrians</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trojan-war">Trojan War</a>. During the sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a> he dragged Cassandra from the statue of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a>, a sacrilege for which the goddess wrecked him on his way home. The Locrians atoned for his crime by sending two noble maidens each year to serve in Athena's temple at Ilion, a custom attested into Roman times.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ajax-the-lesser.jpg" alt="Ajax the Lesser" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kodros Painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Attic_red-figure_cup_with_Ajax_and_Cassandra_Louvre_G_458.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
